      ],
      "source": "https://pagenweb.org/~luzerne/patk/swoy1.htm",
      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The borough incorporated in 1888 after originally being part of Kingston Township chartered by the Susquehanna Company in 1790.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        1
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://pagenweb.org/~luzerne/patk/swoy1.htm",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Coal mining dominated the town until the 1950s, with mines ceasing after the Knox Mine Disaster, yet work continued on Main Street into the 1960s.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
